WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:05.470
Secrets were revealed, questions were answered,
plans were unfurled, and by the time the dust

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:08.580
settled, even secret identities seemed to
be changing hands.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.760
Now we're here to unpack it all.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.740
This is the ending of Watchmen season one,
explained.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:19.520
Though Angela Abar was the clear main character
for much of the series, at least in Tulsa,

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.560
Watchmen also featured two other key law enforcement
officers whose lives were forever tied to

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.140
the events of the original comic.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:31.060
In the HBO series we meet an older version
of Laurie Blake, the second Silk Spectre and

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:35.780
Doctor Manhattan's ex-girlfriend, and Looking
Glass, a Tulsa cop who happened to be near

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:40.260
ground zero on the day Adrian Veidt unleashed
his alien creature to save humanity.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:45.220
As the season ends, both Laurie and LG find
themselves in the same place, with the same

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:50.760
agenda: Arrest Adrian Veidt for his genocidal
crimes, and keep pushing their investigation

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.500
as high as it needs to go, in spite of Veidt's
insistence otherwise.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:58.500
"Because the world will end."

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:00.840
"Yeah.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.780
People keep saying that, but it never seems
to happen."

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.560
So what happens to them next?

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.740
Well, it's easy to see them teaming up on
the future of the Veidt investigation and

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.180
following it all the way through.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:17.010
By the time it's all over, Looking Glass might
even join the FBI, and Laurie might finally

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:20.520
be able to move on from the last shreds of
her superhero past.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:26.020
Watchmen the comic famously reached its climax
with the reveal that Adrian Veidt was behind

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:30.610
the death of the Comedian, and that it was
part of his own massive scheme to "save" humanity

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:33.200
by uniting the world behind a common alien
enemy.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:38.120
To do that, he teleported a giant squid creature
into the heart of New York City, killing three

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.240
million people.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.640
Veidt's bounced around a lot since '85.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.490
He spent a lot of time holed up in his Arctic
sanctuary, Karnak, then was trapped on Europa

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:51.610
for several years, and upon finally returning
to Earth he summoned all of his ego and intellect

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.780
and stopped Lady Trieu from taking Doctor
Manhattan's power.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:59.240
With that in mind, he was convinced he'd be
worshipped as the World's Smartest Man yet

00:01:59.240 --> 00:01:59.740
again.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:04.200
Laurie Blake and Looking Glass had other ideas,
though, and armed with the video Veidt made

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:08.890
for newly elected President Robert Redford
in 1985, they decided to arrest him for the

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:13.689
deaths of the three million in New York, and
for the conspiracy that had continued since,

00:02:13.689 --> 00:02:16.340
via intermittent squid rain engineered by
Veidt.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:21.280
After a strange trial on Europa, Veidt is
presumably headed for another trial on Earth,

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:25.730
but this time he's likely to have plenty of
defenders who hail him as a visionary who

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:28.060
did what he had to in order to save the world.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:32.140
For all we know, Veidt won't even survive
long enough for a trial, but that might be

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:34.400
what Laurie and LG are angling for.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:39.140
As for Redford, who became a co-conspirator
in Veidt's plan when he took office, Blake

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:42.870
makes it clear that it would be fine with
her to bring the president up on charges as

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:47.360
well, which means the United States government
is about to be rocked by a lot of upheaval.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:52.260
Much of Watchmen's season finale is devoted
to explaining exactly what was really going

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:56.620
on with the mysterious Lady Trieu, and it
turns out there's quite a history to mine.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:01.299
Lady Trieu, the Smartest Woman in the World,
was born to a mother who stole a semen sample

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.180
from Adrian Veidt's private vault.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:08.260
Trieu inherited Veidt's intellect, ambition,
and insatiable ego, and it all led her to

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:12.720
believe that she was the only one in the world
worthy of holding Doctor Manhattan's power.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:17.820
"If I can take his power, I can fix the world."

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:22.659
As it turns out, Trieu was planning to kill
Manhattan all along, and her Millennium Clock

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:25.140
housed the device that would have allowed
her to do it.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:29.600
Adrian Veidt was able to stop her at the last
moment with a rain of frozen squid, but while

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.320
Lady Trieu is dead, her legacy is not.

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:37.060
Bian, the clone of Trieu's own mother who
served as her daughter, is still alive, and

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:40.080
her massive corporation and its many holdings
will go to her.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:43.180
Will Bian learn the right lessons from her
mother's hubris?

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:48.099
Will she right the wrongs of Trieu, or will
she in time adopt the same egotistical outlook

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:48.840
on the world?

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:54.080
Lady Trieu's plan to take Doctor Manhattan's
power for herself nearly worked, in part,

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:57.950
because she was using the Seventh Kavalry
plan to also take Doctor Manhattan's power

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:58.700
as cover.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:03.640
The Kavalry, an extension of the racist organization
known as Cyclops that William Reeves spent

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:07.959
nearly all of his adult life fighting, had
been scheming for years to incite an overthrow

00:04:07.959 --> 00:04:12.279
of President Redford, and their fortunes shifted
dramatically when they learned Manhattan was

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:13.080
back on Earth.

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:17.600
Armed with this knowledge and the resources
of Joe Keene Jr., they developed their own

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:20.200
plan to essentially take over the U.S. government.

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:25.460
In the end, their plan failed, and Trieu used
her own resources to vaporize all of Cyclops'

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:28.130
key leadership, including Joe Keene Sr.

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:30.840
The Cyclops is headless, but that doesn't
mean it's dead.

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:35.780
White supremacy has been shown to have a particularly
insidious hold on this world, and it's doubtful

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:38.480
that organized versions of it will vanish
so quickly.

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:43.680
The season finale of Watchmen managed to pack
a lot into its runtime, but one thing the

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:48.160
episode didn't address was the identity of
one of Watchmen's strangest new characters:

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:49.180
"Lube Man."

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:54.420
The character - so named because of his greased,
skin-tight silver suit - appeared only once

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:59.480
in the series proper, and made a very fast
but unforgettable exit via a storm drain.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:04.100
Ever since, fans of the show have been wondering
who exactly was under all that silver.

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:09.930
The season finale didn't tell us, but HBO's
canonical supplement to the series, Peteypedia,

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:11.160
seems to have spelled it out.

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:16.300
The compendium, named for Laurie Blake's FBI
subordinate Dale Petey, hinted in previous

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:20.830
entries that Petey himself may have adopted
the Lube Man identity, and the entries added

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:23.400
after the final episode aired all but confirm
it.

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:28.020
Petey was Lube Man, and he was snooping through
the investigation via his secret identity.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:33.140
Angela Abar's life was forever changed by
the events of Watchmen's first season.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:36.930
She found out the grandfather she never met
was Hooded Justice, and that he was still

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:39.220
alive and still working as a vigilante.

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:41.880
She found out the truth about her friend and
mentor.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:46.660
She had to reveal her husband was secretly
Doctor Manhattan, only to lose him hours later,

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:50.920
and she had to figure out how to pick up the
pieces after Jon died once and for all.

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:55.251
With all this in mind, Watchmen season 1 approaches
its final moments with the promise of a new

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:56.600
beginning for Angela.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:06:01.240
With her children and her grandfather sleeping
safely inside, she walks to her swimming pool

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:06.220
with a miraculously unbroken egg, swallows
it, and remembers something Doctor Manhattan

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:06.880
told her.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:12.740
"So, you can put them in this egg, and if
I ate it, I could walk on water?"

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:17.240
The season stops short of visually confirming
that Manhattan did imbue that last egg with

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:22.221
his powers, therefore passing them on to Angela,
but according to creator Damon Lindelof, there's

00:06:22.221 --> 00:06:23.720
no real ambiguity there.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:28.540
There's no reason to think all those things
Jon said were leading nowhere, and after all...

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:31.760
Angela was bathed in blue light on the poster
for the series.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:36.460
The message is clear: Angela Abar is the new
Doctor Manhattan, whether we got to see her

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:38.020
walk on water or not.

